#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trust Model (Required Reading for Open-Source Deployment)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:13
msgid "FreeAnima is designed for **single-user local / intranet** deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"HTTP / WebUI **has no auth by default**; binding `127.0.0.1` is not security—"
"any process or user that can reach the port can read conversations, send "
"messages, start/stop MCP/ACP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"Default bind is `127.0.0.1`; for LAN access, assess CORS and network "
"isolation yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"**Do not** expose the service to the public internet without reverse-proxy "
"authentication (built-in option: [`remote-access.md`](remote-access.md) — "
"Cloudflare Tunnel + Access)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credential Responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Rule                     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Sole authoritative store | [pass](https://www.passwordstore.org/) (GPG, `~/.password-store`)                                                                                                                                               |\n"
"| Never commit secrets     | Do not write API keys, tokens, DB passwords into `config.yaml` and commit to git                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| Runtime directory        | `~/.anima/` (`FREEANIMA_HOME` overridable) holds config, conversations, memory—recommend `chmod 700`                                                                                                                 |\n"
"| CLI plaintext output     | `anima credential get` prints plaintext to stdout; do not redirect to shared logs                                                                                                                               |\n"
"| WebUI credential detail  | `GET /api/credentials/detail?path=` returns pass plaintext to local WebUI; same sensitivity as CLI; relies on bind address and process isolation                                                                |\n"
"| pass path conventions    | `api/opencode-go`, `services/cloudflare/api-token`, `services/cloudflare/tunnel-credentials`, `services/discord`, `services/firecrawl`, `services/postgres/anima`, `services/pushdeer`, `services/weixin-ilink` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:30
msgid ""
"`config.yaml` supports `credential(\"path\", \"field\")` and `env(\"KEY\")` "
"for secrets (e.g. `database.url: credential(\"services/postgres/anima\", "
"\"url\")` or `env(\"DATABASE_URL\")`); values are injected at runtime from "
"pass or the environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data Persistence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Path                            | Content             | Encryption                      |\n"
"| ------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n"
"| PostgreSQL conversation archive | sessions / messages | No application-layer encryption |\n"
"| `~/.anima/weixin/`              | WeChat sync state   | None                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:39
msgid "Disk backup = data access. Protect backup media accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "LLM Tool Risks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Capability             | Risk                                                                                                           |\n"
"| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `terminal`             | Default `shell: true`, can run arbitrary shell commands                                                        |\n"
"| `file_read_file`       | Partial path deny (`.ssh` private keys, `/etc/passwd`, etc.); **not** full `/etc/` deny                        |\n"
"| `file_write_file`      | deny list + write-protected paths                                                                              |\n"
"| MCP tools              | Capabilities entirely determined by external Server; stdio default, SSE auth scheme not fully defined          |\n"
"| Capability mask (Mask) | Conversation-level tool whitelist; `deny` overrides `allow`; LLM cannot see policy details; see `capabilities/mask` |\n"
"| ACP (Cursor)           | Default **auto-approve** all `session/request_permission` (`allow-once`)                                       |\n"
"| `credentials_list`     | Returns pass path metadata only, no values                                                                     |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measures in Place"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Measure                 | Description                                                                                                        |\n"
"| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Same-origin RPC         | TanStack Start server functions same-origin by default, no CORS whitelist needed                                   |\n"
"| Config secret redaction | `AppRuntime.getConfig()` → `sanitizeConfigForApi()` (`api_key`, `database.url`, nested `pushkey`, `mcp env`, etc.) |\n"
"| MCP config redaction    | `sanitizeMcpConfig`: `env` exposes only `env_keys`                                                                 |\n"
"| Write path safety       | `file_write_file` deny list (partial `/etc/*`, `.ssh` private keys, etc.)                                          |\n"
"| Slash commands          | Whitelist routing                                                                                                  |\n"
"| MCP default stdio       | Reduces port exposure                                                                                              |\n"
"| Credential isolation    | LLM sees pass paths only, not values                                                                               |\n"
"| CI secret scanning      | `.github/workflows/security.yml` (Gitleaks); GitHub Secret scanning + Push protection (free for public repos)      |\n"
"| `.gitignore`            | `.env.*`, `config.yaml`, private key suffixes                                                                      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Known Gaps (Documentation ≠ Fully Implemented)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:69
msgid ""
"The following are planned in code or docs—**deployers must not assume "
"implemented**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Priority | Item                                                  | Status                                                                                                |\n"
"| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| P0       | file_read_file full deny (`/etc/` etc.)               | Partial                                                                                               |\n"
"| P0       | `terminal_run` / `code_execute` default `shell=False` | Not implemented                                                                                       |\n"
"| P1       | Runtime Unix socket `chmod 600` + handshake token     | Not implemented                                                                                       |\n"
"| P1       | `FREEANIMA_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT` / `READ_SAFE_ROOT`        | Not implemented                                                                                       |\n"
"| P2       | HTTP API auth                                         | None by default; Cloudflare Access JWT when `tunnel.enabled` ([`remote-access.md`](remote-access.md)) |\n"
"| P3       | IPC / LLM rate limiting                               | None                                                                                                  |\n"
"| P3       | Session disk encryption                               | None                                                                                                  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "Threat Sources"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code  | Name                | Description                                                      |\n"
"| ----- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **A** | External attack     | Unauthorized access, port exposure                               |\n"
"| **B** | LLM-layer injection | Prompt injection, tool parameter manipulation, command injection |\n"
"| **C** | Agent error         | Mistaken dangerous operations                                    |\n"
"| **D** | Dependency chain    | Third-party lib / MCP / ACP compromise                           |\n"
"| **E** | Data security       | Conversation leak, key leak, memory tampering                    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security Matrix"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module           | A External                                      | B LLM injection                                                     | C Agent error             | D Dependencies     | E Data                             |\n"
"| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Runtime**      | Default 127.0.0.1 bind                          | MaxTurnsExceeded                                                    | Gap: rate limiting        | llm client vulns   | PG unencrypted                     |\n"
"| **Gateway**      | Token in pass                                   | Malicious messages                                                  | Reply with sensitive info | SDK vulns          | —                                  |\n"
"| **CLI / Tools**  | Local shell compromised                         | file_read_file partial deny (**P0 extending**); shell=True (**P0**) | rm -rf etc.               | —                  | Logs may contain conversations     |\n"
"| **HTTP / WebUI** | No auth by default; tunnel mode uses Access JWT | BFF does not touch LLM params directly                              | config display            | Vue/axios          | SSE plaintext                      |\n"
"| **MCP / ACP**    | SSE auth undefined                              | Malicious params                                                    | Wrong delegation          | Server compromised | Context may contain sensitive data |\n"
msgstr ""

